course: dictionary
lesson: 74
title: The Acropolis
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names of real places. When you meet a name you do not know, look at the words around it for clues. «Athens was a city of traders, sailors, thinkers and artists, with the Parthenon temple to the goddess Athena on its rocky hill, the Acropolis.» The clues are rocky hill and temple, so the Acropolis must be a place: a hill with a temple on top.
explain: Look at the capital letter. «The Acropolis» is a proper noun, the name of one special place in Athens, Greece. A small-letter «acropolis» is a common noun, and it means the high, fortified part of any ancient Greek city.
explain: Fortified means it had strong walls or defences to keep enemies out. So the high part of a city was both a safe place and a place to see far. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «on its rocky hill, the high fortified part of Athens» still makes sense.
fact: The Acropolis is a rocky hill in Athens, Greece.
fact: On top of the Acropolis stand ancient temples, including the Parthenon.
fact: The Parthenon was a temple to the goddess Athena.
fact: An acropolis is the high, fortified part of any ancient Greek city.
fact: You will often meet the phrases «the Acropolis of Athens» and «on the Acropolis».
exercise: «Athens was a city of traders, sailors, thinkers and artists, with the Parthenon temple to the goddess Athena on its rocky hill, the Acropolis.» What is the Acropolis? | *A rocky hill in Athens with ancient temples on top | A type of Greek statue | A sea port where the sailors kept their boats | A market where traders sold food
exercise: Find and copy the name of the goddess in the sentence. | Parthenon | *Athena | traders | Athens
exercise: What does a small-letter acropolis mean? | A kind of ancient Greek boat | *The high, fortified part of any ancient Greek city | A modern shopping centre | A rocky hill in Athens named after a goddess
test: «The students climbed to the top of the Acropolis to see the Parthenon.» Where did the students climb? | The Parthenon's shop | A market in the city centre | A harbour full of sailors | *The rocky hill with ancient temples on top
test: Why was an acropolis built high up and with strong walls? | To keep the sailors' boats dry | Because the goddess Athena asked for a swimming pool | *To be a safe place and to see far over the city | To make a fine place for shopping
exam: Read the clues: «on its rocky hill» and «the Parthenon temple». What does the word Acropolis mean in this sentence? | *A rocky hill in Athens with ancient temples on top | A kind of Greek coin | A busy harbour for traders | A goddess who lived in Athens
